many benefits for our staff. Avondale is committed to creating a safe space for all staff, students and community members. As part of the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025, Avondale will consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of the recruitment process. As part of the recruitment process, candidates who progress to the interview stage will need to complete and return the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form. Other forms may include a Working with Children Check, Police Check or any other pre-employment checks appropriate to the role. Avondale University Positions Cultural Support Officer Director of Student Services Learning and Teaching Support Officer 7@Avondale Positions Contact People and Culture at Avondale University. Visit Adventist Employment for positions vacant at other entities of the Seventh-day Adventist Church in the South Pacific . Adventist Employment Student Employment Avondale University employs students on a casual basis for help in various roles. Students seeking casual employment should complete the Student Worker Application . Employment will require the provision of Avondale’s Student Engagement Form, bank account details and a taxation declaration. Students can obtain these forms from each department once employment is offered. Student Worker Application ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Email Address: * Email Address Confirm Email Address I am.. * Select... a High School Student a Parent/Guardian a Teacher looking at postgraduate study other Current School Year: * Select... Year 12 Year 11 Year 10 Year 9 Other I am interested in: * Select... Arts (Chaplaincy, Communications, Counselling, English, History, Music, Psychology, Visual Art) Business Individual Support 