    "https://www.avondale.edu.au/job/associate-lecturer-or-lecturer-counselling/": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (Counselling)",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (Counselling) - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Lifestyle Medicine & Health Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Avondale » Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (Counselling) Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (Counselling) Lake Macquarie Campus, NSW Part-time (15 hrs per week) Fixed-term contract (February - December 2027) Avondale University has a part-time, fixed-term opportunity to join the School of Arts & Business in our Counselling specialty, to back-fill a period of leave. Be part of the transformation Avondale University is a Seventh-day Adventist organisation driven by its mission and values. If you share this passion for supporting the delivery of Christian tertiary education and can align with this mission, ethos and lifestyle principles, then you are encouraged to apply. The level of appointment will be determined on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. What will you do? As an Associate Lecturer or Lecturer in our Counselling program, you will be involved in teaching and Clinical Coordination. Typical duties will include: Deliver high-quality teaching and learning experiences in the counselling discipline. Facilitate engaging classroom, online and blended learning environments that promote student participation, critical thinking and professional development. Assess student learning outcomes and provide timely, constructive feedback to support academic success. Coordinate counselling practicum and field placements, providing guidance and support to students and placement supervisors and ensuring successful completion of placement requirements. Maintain current knowledge of counselling theory, practice, ethics and relevant legislation, integrating contemporary developments into teaching activities. Contributing to the administrative duties of the School of Arts & Business. Essential criteria: Master’s degree in a relevant field; A minimum of five years demonstrated clinical counselling experience; Demonstrated experience in clinical supervision; Proven ability to support the professional development of emerging practitioners through reflective practice, case consultation, skills development and performance feedback; Demonstrated ability and willingness to work as a team member; and Supportive of the mission, values and ethos of Avondale. Desirable criteria: Demonstrated experience in inspiring and motivating student engagement. Doctoral degree in a relevant field. Why Work at Avondale? Values-driven organisation Compressed working week with half day Friday’s Heavily discounted further study options Discounted school fees for attendance at Adventist schools Free access to Avondale Libraries Please visit www.avondale.edu.au/employment for the full selection criteria and level descriptors for this position. For further information about the role, please email [email protected] . Email your application to [email protected] , including: A resume A statement addressing the selection criteria Contact details of three referees Applications close on 24 October 2026 Please note that we will be conducting interviews as applications come in, so please do not delay in submitting your application. Avondale is an equal opportunity employer and reserves the right to make a delayed appointment, not to appoint, or to appoint by invitation. Download Job Description ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Email Address: * Email Address Confirm Email Address I am.. * Select... a High School Student a Parent/Guardian a Teacher looking at postgraduate study other Current School Year: * Select... Year 12 Year 11 Year 10 Year 9 Other I am interested in: * Select... Arts (Chaplaincy, Communications, Counselling, English, History, Music, Psychology, Visual Art) Business Individual Support Lifestyle Medicine Ministry & Theology Nursing Outdoor Leadership Science Research Degrees Teaching Unsure/Other How did you hear about us? * Select... At School Bus Advertisement Career Expos Church/Church Big Camps Good Universities Guide Google Printed material (course guide, leaflet, brochure) Radio Record Magazine Social Media (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIN) UAC website Word of Mouth (friends, family, teachers) Other Your message: * By submitting this form, you consent to Avondale University collecting your information for the purpose of responding to your enquiry and providing relevant information about the University. Your information will remain confidential and will not be shared with third parties. Submit About Us Who We Are History Our Purpose Campuses Research Jobs Policies Online Store Terms of Use Copyright Study Courses International Students Student Profile Fees and Costs Scholarships Gettin